  "interpretation": "The Phase-0 Cartesian (mixed-radix) universe is the correct model for CATEGORICAL formulation axes but is a strict, and severely wasteful, superset once composition axes are closed (sum(x)=1). Filtering the Cartesian grid by closure reproduces the Scheffe {q,m} simplex-lattice exactly, so the lattice generator is a loss-free replacement at a small fraction of the cardinality. For bounded coating regions the extreme-vertex set is confirmed by two independent published algorithms and pinned by the Piepel 1983 implied-bound range identity.",
